<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77215" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰν-άκεια</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>universal remedy, panacea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				38.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.215
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.766
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> name of <i>a
				healing herb</i> or <i>its juice</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανακής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				40
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανακείας ῥίζα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					14.156
				</span></i>
			; <i>Hercules' woundwort, Opopanax hispidus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.15.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγυστικόν</span>
			, <i>Laserpitium garganicum</i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.106
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i>six, Theol. Ar.</i><i><span class="en">
				38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> personified
			as daughter of Asclepius, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Jusj.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				702
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				730
			</span></i>.</div>
